WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Speaker 1: Let's talk a little more about this&nbsp;
loyalty pledge that Republicans and the Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.280
National Committee want. Every candidate who&nbsp;
is vying for the Republican primary to sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.780
in advance of participating in any debates.&nbsp;
We talked about this last week. Many of you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.400
wrote to me about it and we have more about&nbsp;
it. I'll remind you what's going on. The RNC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.040
and the Republican Party want every single&nbsp;
candidate who's running to agree in advance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.980
Even if I lose, I will support whoever is&nbsp;
eventually the Republican nominee. Really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:38.460
the concern here is Trump. Why? Well, Trump is&nbsp;
a child and Trump puts himself above everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:44.460
above party, above everything. And so it's a&nbsp;
legitimate risk to the Republican Party that Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.920
might run in the Republican primary, but lose.&nbsp;
Maybe DeSantis wins. Maybe. Who knows? Somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.000
else wins. And then Trump, instead of saying,&nbsp;
Hey, you know what, I lost fair and square,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.200
I'm going to support the person that won. I mean,&nbsp;
it's like laughable that he would do that, right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.580
Trump instead will say, well, you know what? It&nbsp;
was stolen. It was rigged, and I'm going to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.880
as an independent and show these Republicans&nbsp;
whose boss and the reason that this would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.320
so devastating to the party is there are so&nbsp;
many states where the margins are always thin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.100
whether it's a Republican or a Democrat who&nbsp;
wins everything from Florida, Pennsylvania,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.740
Ohio, Michigan, Wisconsin, Arizona. There's&nbsp;
so many states where it's always pretty close.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:27.840
If Trump ran as an independent and took just 5 to&nbsp;
7% of the Republican vote, it would guarantee that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.680
the Democratic candidate wins. Trump, running&nbsp;
as an independent, could guarantee one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.860
biggest Democratic victories in 2024 that we've&nbsp;
seen in decades. So they've asked him to sign a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.220
loyalty pledge. They're asking everybody to sign&nbsp;
a loyalty pledge. And one of the things that came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.200
up last week was Trump isn't going to do this.&nbsp;
But now there's a different perspective. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.260
the perspective for many of you is, oh, Trump&nbsp;
will do it. He just won't abide by it. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:57.540
on CNN, Ronna McDaniel was asked by&nbsp;
Dana Bash about this entire loyalty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:01.800
pledge scenario. And here's what she had to say.
